      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently on the android15-6.6-desktop branch the kvm doesn\u0027t use cma, that\u0027s correct. The problematic part is after merging the android15-6.6 branch (which is a part of a 3-way merge process of syncing android15-6.6-dsktop branch) where kvm uses `cma_alloc` function - take a look here:\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android15-6.6/arch/arm64/kvm/iommu.c#73\n\n\nOnce I merge this branch the compilation for arm64 fails on linking as these functions can\u0027t be found.\nAs per the dependencies - I was wondering about it too, shouldn\u0027t there be an entry here:\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android15-6.6/arch/arm64/kvm/Kconfig#23\n\nwith `select CONFIG_CMA` to provide all required dependencies?",
