      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, thanks. So the CMA dependency was introduced by aosp/3425886, which is a pKVM change, but since KVM on arm64 enables pKVM compilation unconditionally, it makes the entire KVM dependent on CMA.\n\n\u003e As per the dependencies - I was wondering about it too, shouldn\u0027t there be an entry here:\n\u003e\n\u003e https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android15-6.6/arch/arm64/kvm/Kconfig#23\n\u003e\n\u003e with select CONFIG_CMA to provide all required dependencies?\n\nYeah, that seems like the proper fix to do... OTOH, this part of pKVM is not in upstream yet, so as long as it remains Android-only, perhaps it\u0027s fine to keep things as is (as Android enables CMA anyway).\n\nCC\u0027ing @vdonnefort@google.com who is the author of aosp/3425886.\n\n...In the meantime, this CL looks good to me (after all, what it does is just align the legacy config with gki_defconfig).",
